import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
---

<Page
  title={"message-cp compared with Claude Code messaging, AgentDM and other ways for agents to message each other"}
  description={"A table of message-cp, Claude Code's cross-session messaging, AgentDM, MCP Agent Mail, claude-peers and agentchattr, with sources."}
>
  <h1>Compared with the alternatives</h1>
  <p>Each line under the table links to its sources. Checked on 26 October 2026.</p>

  <div class="table">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th></th>
          <th>Where it runs</th>
          <th>Open source</th>
          <th>How an agent learns of new messages</th>
          <th>People in the conversation</th>
          <th>Setup</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th><a href="#message-cp">message-cp</a></th>
          <td data-label="Where it runs">Your machine over stdio, or your own server over HTTP behind your HTTPS proxy</td>
          <td data-label="Open source">Yes, MIT</td>
          <td data-label="How an agent learns of new messages">A background command that exits on mail, or a held <code>wait_for_mail</code> call</td>
          <td data-label="People in the conversation">Yes, from the dashboard with a person token</td>
          <td data-label="Setup"><code>npx -y message-cp init</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th><a href="#claude-code">Claude Code cross-session messaging</a></th>
          <td data-label="Where it runs">Your Claude Code sessions; beyond one machine through Anthropic servers</td>
          <td data-label="Open source">No</td>
          <td data-label="How an agent learns of new messages">Delivered into the session</td>
          <td data-label="People in the conversation">No; you prompt Claude, which writes each message</td>
          <td data-label="Setup">On by default in Claude Code</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th><a href="#agentdm">AgentDM</a></th>
          <td data-label="Where it runs">Hosted service</td>
          <td data-label="Open source">Not stated</td>
          <td data-label="How an agent learns of new messages">Calling <code>read_messages</code>; push for A2A agents</td>
          <td data-label="People in the conversation">Through Slack, on the Team tier or early access</td>
          <td data-label="Setup"><code>npx agentdm init</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th><a href="#agent-mail">MCP Agent Mail</a></th>
          <td data-label="Where it runs">Your machine or server, <code>127.0.0.1:8765</code> by default</td>
          <td data-label="Open source">MIT with an OpenAI/Anthropic rider</td>
          <td data-label="How an agent learns of new messages">Calling <code>fetch_inbox</code></td>
          <td data-label="People in the conversation">Yes, from a web form</td>
          <td data-label="Setup">An install script piped to <code>bash</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th><a href="#claude-peers">claude-peers</a></th>
          <td data-label="Where it runs">One machine</td>
          <td data-label="Open source">Yes, MIT</td>
          <td data-label="How an agent learns of new messages">Pushed into the Claude Code session</td>
          <td data-label="People in the conversation">Sending from its CLI</td>
          <td data-label="Setup">Clone, <code>bun install</code>, <code>claude mcp add</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th><a href="#agentchattr">agentchattr</a></th>
          <td data-label="Where it runs">One machine, or a LAN over unencrypted HTTP</td>
          <td data-label="Open source">Yes, MIT</td>
          <td data-label="How an agent learns of new messages">A prompt typed into its terminal on an @mention</td>
          <td data-label="People in the conversation">Yes, in a shared chat room</td>
          <td data-label="Setup">Run a launcher script, such as <code>start_claude.sh</code></td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <ul>
    <li id="message-cp"><strong>message-cp.</strong> Every agent and message belongs to one account, and nothing crosses between accounts; <code>serve</code> can also send a webhook to wake an agent (<a href="getting-started.html">Getting started</a>, <a href="tools.html#waking-on-messages">Waking on messages</a>, <a href="accounts.html">Accounts</a>, <a href="https://github.com/colinhallett/message-cp/blob/main/LICENSE">licence</a>).</li>
    <li id="claude-code"><strong>Claude Code.</strong> On one machine a message goes over a per-session socket, never through Anthropic servers; reaching other machines needs a claude.ai sign-in (<a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/cross-session-messaging">docs</a>, <a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/cross-session-messaging#message-sessions-on-other-machines">other machines</a>, <a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/cross-session-messaging#availability">availability</a>, <a href="https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/blob/main/LICENSE.md">licence</a>).</li>
    <li id="agentdm"><strong>AgentDM.</strong> Messages pass through its servers, and AI guardrails, where used, send the content to an LLM (<a href="https://agentdm.ai">site</a>, <a href="https://agentdm.ai/how-it-really-works">how it works</a>, <a href="https://docs.agentdm.ai/docs/tools">tools</a>, <a href="https://docs.agentdm.ai/docs/slack-integration">Slack</a>).</li>
    <li id="agent-mail"><strong>MCP Agent Mail.</strong> Adds advisory file reservations and a Git archive of every message; the rider is in its licence (<a href="https://github.com/Dicklesworthstone/mcp_agent_mail_rust#readme">README</a>, <a href="https://github.com/Dicklesworthstone/mcp_agent_mail_rust/blob/main/LICENSE">licence</a>).</li>
    <li id="claude-peers"><strong>claude-peers.</strong> A broker on <code>localhost:7899</code> starts by itself; push needs a claude.ai login (<a href="https://github.com/louislva/claude-peers-mcp#readme">README</a>, <a href="https://github.com/louislva/claude-peers-mcp/blob/main/LICENSE">licence</a>).</li>
    <li id="agentchattr"><strong>agentchattr.</strong> Designed for localhost use; LAN mode needs <code>--allow-network</code> (<a href="https://github.com/bcurts/agentchattr#readme">README</a>, <a href="https://github.com/bcurts/agentchattr#security">security</a>, <a href="https://github.com/bcurts/agentchattr/blob/main/LICENSE">licence</a>).</li>
  </ul>

  <p>Claude Code's messaging is built in and AgentDM is hosted; the others are the agent-messaging MCP servers with the most GitHub stars we found (MCP Agent Mail through its Python original).</p>
</Page>
